{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>That he not turn aside from the commandment.</b> Even a minor commandment of a prophet." "<b>That his days may be long.</b> From the affirmative you infer the negative. So we find with Saul: Samuel said to him (I Samuel 10), ״Seven days you shall wait until I come to you,״ to offer burnt offerings — and it is written (I Samuel 13), ״And he waited seven days,״ and he did not keep to his appointed time for the whole day, and he did not manage to offer the burnt offering before Samuel came and said to him, ״You have acted foolishly; you did not keep … and now your kingdom shall not stand״ — thus you learn that for a minor commandment of a prophet he was punished." "<b>He and his sons.</b> This teaches that if his son is fit for kingship, he takes precedence over anyone. (Horayot 11)"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:32.050621347Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}